From 4d108a47d86e1ffac923d43b241fca993a2412de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Apr 2023 13:59:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] clk: hisilicon: use the split clock headers

The CRG driver of each SoC provides different clocks and resets, so one
generic header across all HiSTB SoCs is wrong.

Split histb-clock.h into hisilicon,hi3798cv200-crg.h and

hisilicon,hi3798cv200-sysctrl.h and keep histb-clock.h as a deprecated
wrapper that includes both for backward compatibility only.

Include the individual headers from the in-tree consumers,

crg-hi3798cv200.c and the poplar dtsi, so neither prints the deprecation
warning.

Acked-by: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@linaro.org>
Signed-off-by: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/hisilicon/crg-hi3798cv200.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/clk/hisilicon/crg-hi3798cv200.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/hisilicon/crg-hi3798cv200.c
@@ -5,7 +5,8 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2016 HiSilicon Technologies Co., Ltd.
  */
 
-#include <dt-bindings/clock/histb-clock.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-crg.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-sysctrl.h>
 #include <linux/clk-provider.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
